---
import StatePage from '../../layouts/StatePage.astro';
---
<StatePage
  title="About SmallEstateForm.com — Estate Document Generator"
  description="SmallEstateForm.com is a free estate document generator built for grieving families. Current 2026 law, county-level specificity, and a bank instruction letter included free."
  canonicalUrl="https://smallestateform.com/about/"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section style="background:linear-gradient(140deg,#2D5016,#1E3A0F);padding:5rem 1.5rem 4rem;text-align:center;">
    <div style="max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;">
      <div style="display:inline-block;border:1px solid rgba(247,244,239,0.2);color:rgba(247,244,239,0.7);font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:0.35rem 1rem;border-radius:100px;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our mission</div>
      <h1 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.2rem);color:#F7F4EF;margin-bottom:1.25rem;line-height:1.2;">Built for families,<br>not lawyers.</h1>
      <p style="color:rgba(247,244,239,0.7);font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.65;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto;">When someone you love dies, the last thing you should have to navigate is a mountain of outdated paperwork and overpriced attorneys. We built SmallEstateForm.com to change that.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Mission -->
  <section style="padding:4rem 1.5rem;background:#F7F4EF;border-bottom:1px solid #D4CCC0;">
    <div style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;">
      <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:2rem;color:#2C2C2A;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Why we exist</h2>
      <p style="font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;color:#2C2C2A;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1rem;">Every year, 2.8 million Americans die. Their families — already grieving — discover that accessing even small estate assets requires legal documents. They search online, find templates that are years out of date, download them, and hand them to banks that reject them.</p>
      <p style="font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;color:#2C2C2A;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1rem;">The gap between "what the law says" and "what the internet offers" is enormous. Arizona's limits changed in March 2026. Illinois amended its Probate Act in August 2025. California raised its threshold in April 2026. The PDF at the top of Google for "small estate affidavit illinois" is from 2015.</p>
      <p style="font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;color:#2C2C2A;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1rem;background:#EEF4E8;border-left:3px solid #2D5016;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.9rem;"><strong>SmallEstateForm.com is the only generator built on current 2026 law</strong> — with real county-level specificity and a bank instruction letter that compels banks to cooperate. Free during beta.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Values -->
  <section style="padding:4rem 1.5rem;background:#EEE9E1;border-bottom:1px solid #D4CCC0;">
    <div style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;">
      <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:2rem;color:#2C2C2A;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">What we believe</h2>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:1.5rem;">
        <div style="background:white;border:1px solid #D4CCC0;border-top:3px solid #2D5016;padding:1.5rem;">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.25rem;color:#2C2C2A;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Current law, always</h3>
          <p style="font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.875rem;color:#6B6560;line-height:1.6;">Every document reflects the law as it exists today — not when a competitor last updated their template. We track state amendments so you don't have to.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:white;border:1px solid #D4CCC0;border-top:3px solid #2D5016;padding:1.5rem;">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.25rem;color:#2C2C2A;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Your privacy matters</h3>
          <p style="font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.875rem;color:#6B6560;line-height:1.6;">All document generation happens in your browser. The name of the deceased, heir information, and asset details are never uploaded to our servers.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:white;border:1px solid #D4CCC0;border-top:3px solid #8B6914;padding:1.5rem;">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.25rem;color:#2C2C2A;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Honest about limits</h3>
          <p style="font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.875rem;color:#6B6560;line-height:1.6;">We are document generators, not attorneys. For complicated estates — disputed heirs, significant debts, property over the threshold — we always recommend consulting a lawyer.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:white;border:1px solid #D4CCC0;border-top:3px solid #8B6914;padding:1.5rem;">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.25rem;color:#2C2C2A;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Fair price</h3>
          <p style="font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.875rem;color:#6B6560;line-height:1.6;">$19.99 for a document that saves $3,000–$20,000 in probate attorney fees. Free during beta. No subscription, no account, no data harvesting.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Documents covered -->
  <section style="padding:4rem 1.5rem;background:#F7F4EF;border-bottom:1px solid #D4CCC0;">
    <div style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;">
      <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:2rem;color:#2C2C2A;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Documents we generate</h2>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:1rem;">
        <div style="border:1px solid #D4CCC0;padding:1.25rem;border-radius:4px;background:white;">
          <div style="color:#8B6914;font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;margin-bottom:0.5rem;font-weight:500;">Texas</div>
          <div style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Affidavit of Heirship</div>
          <div style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#6B6560;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;">Texas Estates Code Chapter 203 · No threshold · Two disinterested witnesses</div>
        </div>
        <div style="border:1px solid #D4CCC0;padding:1.25rem;border-radius:4px;background:white;">
          <div style="color:#8B6914;font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;margin-bottom:0.5rem;font-weight:500;">Arizona · HB2116 March 2026</div>
          <div style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Small Estate Affidavit</div>
          <div style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#6B6560;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;">ARS §14-3971 · $200K personal / $300K real · County-specific forms</div>
        </div>
        <div style="border:1px solid #D4CCC0;padding:1.25rem;border-radius:4px;background:white;">
          <div style="color:#8B6914;font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;margin-bottom:0.5rem;font-weight:500;">Illinois · August 2025</div>
          <div style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Small Estate Affidavit</div>
          <div style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#6B6560;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;">755 ILCS 5/25-1 · $150K statewide · Cook County separate formula</div>
        </div>
        <div style="border:1px solid #D4CCC0;padding:1.25rem;border-radius:4px;background:white;">
          <div style="color:#8B6914;font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;margin-bottom:0.5rem;font-weight:500;">California</div>
          <div style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Transfer on Death Deed</div>
          <div style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#6B6560;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;">Civil Code §5600–5696 · AB 1052 · Any CA real property · Plan ahead</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.875rem;color:#6B6560;margin-top:1.5rem;">Additional states launching monthly. <a href="/small-estate-affidavit/" style="color:#8B6914;text-decoration:none;">See the full state guide →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section style="background:#2D5016;padding:4rem 1.5rem;text-align:center;">
    <div style="max-width:500px;margin:0 auto;">
      <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:2rem;color:#F7F4EF;margin-bottom:1rem;">Ready to get started?</h2>
      <p style="font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;color:rgba(247,244,239,0.65);margin-bottom:2rem;line-height:1.6;">Select your state and generate a legally correct estate document in minutes. Free during beta.</p>
      <a href="/" style="display:inline-block;background:#8B6914;color:white;padding:1rem 2.5rem;border-radius:3px;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.95rem;font-weight:500;text-decoration:none;">Generate Your Document →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</StatePage>
